{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 1449,
    "dDurationMs": 3781,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you’re riding a bike and want to turn\nright, you might think that you should turn"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5230,
    "dDurationMs": 1439,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the handlebars to the right."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 6669,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "However, that’s wrong."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 8109,
    "dDurationMs": 4391,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because, unlike a car where turning the wheels\nmerely changes the direction the car is pointed,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12500,
    "dDurationMs": 2140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "turning the front wheel makes a bike lean."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 14640,
    "dDurationMs": 3650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When you turn the bike wheel to the right,\nthe wheel goes to the right, right out from"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 18290,
    "dDurationMs": 1750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "under you and the rest of the bike."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 20040,
    "dDurationMs": 3070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So now you’re leaning to the left, and the\nforce on the bike from the ground will be"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 23110,
    "dDurationMs": 4230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "directed to the left, and a leftward force,\nof course, makes you go to the left."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 27340,
    "dDurationMs": 3310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Since physics seems determined that you’re\ngoing left, you’d probably better just give"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 30650,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in and let the handlebars turn to the left,\ntoo."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 33210,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that’s how you turn left on a bike – by\nfirst turning right."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 36370,
    "dDurationMs": 3910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you really wanted to go right, you should\nhave started by counter-steering to the left."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 40280,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Once you finally get yourself into a right\nturn, you’ll also need to work to keep yourself"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 44440,
    "dDurationMs": 3710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the turn, since most bikes and motorcycles\nhave a tendency to automatically stabilize"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 48150,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and straighten out on their own."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 49710,
    "dDurationMs": 3860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This happens because a right-leaning bike\nautomatically steers itself even farther to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 53570,
    "dDurationMs": 3470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the right to get the wheels back underneath\nits center of mass, so you’ll actually need"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 57040,
    "dDurationMs": 4199,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to apply a slight torque to the left to keep\nthe wheels from turning too far to the right."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 61239,
    "dDurationMs": 4650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yes, it’s counterintuitive: to turn right\non a bike you turn left, then keep trying"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 65889,
    "dDurationMs": 3031,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to turn left while leaning and turning right."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 68920,
    "dDurationMs": 28769,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Bikes "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 97689,
    "dDurationMs": 8901,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are weird."
    } ]
  } ]
}
